[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:What's for Supper?]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.32]What kind of fish are they? | 它们是哪种鱼？
[00:14.64]Fish and chips has always been a favourite dish in Britain, | 油炸鱼加炸薯条一直是英国人喜爱的一道菜，
[00:19.85]but as the oceans have been overfished, fish has become more and more expensive. | 但是由于海洋捕捞过度，鱼变得越来越贵。
[00:27.29]So it comes as a surprise to learn that giant fish are terrifying the divers on North Sea oil rigs. | 因此，当得知北海石油钻井平台上的潜水员正被巨型鱼吓坏时，人们感到很意外。
[00:37.30]Oil rigs have to be repaired frequently and divers, who often have to work in darkness a hundred feet under water, | 钻井平台需要经常维修，潜水员常常要在水下100英尺的黑暗中工作，
[00:47.27]have been frightened out of their wits by giant fish bumping into them as they work. | 工作时常被撞到他们身上的大鱼吓得魂不附体。
[00:54.83]Now they have had special cages made to protect them from these monsters. | 现在他们造了特制的笼子，用来保护自己免受这些怪物的伤害。
[01:01.06]The fish are not sharks or killer whales, | 这些鱼并不是鲨鱼或逆戟鲸，
[01:05.12]but favourite eating varieties like cod and skate which grow to unnatural sizes, | 而是深受人们喜爱的食用品种，如鳕鱼和鳐鱼，只是它们长得异乎寻常地大，
[01:12.92]sometimes as much as twelve feet in length. | 有时长达12英尺。
[01:17.85]Three factors have caused these fish to grow so large: | 造成这些鱼长得如此之大的因素有三个：
[01:23.01]the warm water round the hot oil pipes under the sea; | 海底热油管周围的温水；
[01:28.17]the plentiful supply of food thrown overboard by the crews on the rigs; | 钻井平台上的工作人员抛入海中的大量食物；
[01:34.73]the total absence of fishing boats around the oil rigs. | 钻井平台周围完全没有渔船。
[01:39.95]As a result, the fish just eat and eat and grow and grow in the lovely warm water. | 结果，这些鱼就在可爱的温水中吃了又吃，长了又长。
[01:49.24]Who eats who? | 谁吃谁呢？
